# Zustand Store Patterns

## Store Structure

All stores use `persist` + `devtools` middleware:

```typescript
export const useXxxStore = create<XxxState>()(
  devtools(
    persist(
      (set) => ({ /* state */ }),
      { name: 'xxx-storage' },   // localStorage key
    ),
    { name: 'XxxStore' },        // devtools label
  ),
);
```

## Hydration-Safe Hooks

Client components that read persisted state must guard against SSR/hydration mismatch:

```typescript
const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false);
useEffect(() => { setMounted(true); }, []);

const safeValue = mounted ? storeValue : defaultValue;
```

## Existing Stores

| Store | File | localStorage key |
|-------|------|-----------------|
| Cart | `shared/store/cart-store.ts` | `noview-shop-cart-storage` |
| Auth | `shared/store/auth-store.ts` | `noview-shop-auth-storage` |
| Shipping | `shared/store/shipping-store.ts` | `noview-shop-shipping-storage` |
| Language | `shared/store/lang-store.ts` | `noview-shop-lang-storage` |
| Wishlist | `shared/store/wishlist-store.ts` | `noview-shop-wishlist-storage` |

## Shared Hooks (wrapping stores)

Don't consume stores directly in components when a wrapper hook already exists:

| Hook | File | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| `useCart()` | `shared/hooks/use-cart.ts` | Hydration-safe cart count + actions |
| `useWishlist()` | `shared/hooks/use-wishlist.ts` | Auth-gated wishlist per user → redirects to `/login` |
| `useWishlistItems()` | `shared/hooks/use-wishlist-items.ts` | Resolves full `CategoryItem[]` from wishlist IDs |
| `useT()` | `shared/hooks/use-t.ts` | Current language translations |

## Rules

- Never call `localStorage` directly — use Zustand persist
- Never add state to component that belongs in a store
- Export store hook directly (`useXxxStore`), wrap for hydration safety in `shared/hooks/`
- Prefer shared hooks over direct store access in components
- All localStorage keys must be prefixed with `noview-shop-`
